This diff should log every key input:

````
diff --git a/helix-term/src/ui/editor.rs b/helix-term/src/ui/editor.rs
index 3626c5ddc..a046fc087 100644
--- a/helix-term/src/ui/editor.rs
+++ b/helix-term/src/ui/editor.rs
@@ -1469,6 +1469,7 @@ fn handle_event(
                 EventResult::Consumed(None)
             }
             Event::Key(mut key) => {
+                log::warn!("Key: {:?}", key);
                 cx.editor.reset_idle_timer();
                 canonicalize_key(&mut key);
````

Or you can pull this branch: https://github.com/participant1/helix/tree/push-unmwtturkuzo

If you don't see something like this in your log:

````
helix_term::ui::editor [WARN] Key: KeyEvent { code: Char('i'), modifiers: KeyModifiers(0x0) }
````

then helix can't receive any key events from the terminal.

I could replicate this bug with `aerc`, looks like it was introduced in 253e619. Specifically, this part: https://github.com/helix-editor/helix/blob/e7874bc69c0549fe87e863c4b4f6a5c2fccffca7/helix-tui/src/backend/termina.rs#L136-L139

Looks like some terminals just don't play well with OSC 11 at all. 

@reporter: I would appreciate if you could test this branch with default macOS terminal: https://github.com/participant1/helix/tree/push-xsxotyrvyvvz
